---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import ProjectHero from "../../components/ProjectHero.astro";

const technologies = [
  "Python",
  "OpenCV",
  "scikit-image",
  "Image Processing",
  "Computer Vision",
  "Optimization",
  "MecSimCalc",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rooftop Solar Panel Optimization | Daniela Chanta"
  description="Computer-vision and optimization pipeline for rooftop analysis and photovoltaic panel placement developed during the University of Alberta Research Experience."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main>

    <!-- HERO -->

    <ProjectHero
      category="Computer Vision · Optimization · Engineering"
      title="Rooftop Solar Panel Optimization"
      description="A computer-vision and optimization pipeline for analyzing rooftop geometry, estimating feasible photovoltaic panel placement and supporting engineering decision-making."
      year="2024"
      role="Research Intern / Developer"
      organization="University of Alberta"
      technologies={technologies}
    />


    <!-- OVERVIEW -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>
          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            Overview
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Automating part of the photovoltaic design workflow.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-8 text-slate-600">

          <p>
            This project was developed during the University of Alberta
            Research Experience and explored how image processing and
            optimization techniques could support rooftop photovoltaic
            analysis.
          </p>

          <p>
            The objective was to process rooftop imagery and geometric
            information in Python, identify usable roof regions, evaluate panel
            placement constraints and estimate possible photovoltaic layouts.
          </p>

          <p>
            The resulting workflow combined computer vision with engineering
            constraints so that visual information could be transformed into
            a structured decision-support process.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- PROBLEM -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>
          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            The Problem
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Rooftop solar design requires reasoning about geometry, constraints and energy potential.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6 leading-8 text-slate-600">

          <p>
            Evaluating whether a rooftop is suitable for photovoltaic
            installation is not only a matter of measuring total surface area.
            The usable region can be affected by roof shape, orientation,
            boundaries and placement constraints.
          </p>

          <p>
            A manual evaluation can become repetitive when many rooftops or
            different panel configurations must be considered.
          </p>

          <p>
            The project investigated how image-processing techniques could
            automate geometric analysis and provide inputs for panel-placement
            optimization.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- PIPELINE -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="max-w-3xl">

        <p
          class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
        >
          Pipeline
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
        >
          From rooftop imagery to panel-layout candidates.
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 leading-8 text-slate-600">
          The workflow combined image analysis, geometric processing and
          optimization to convert rooftop information into feasible solar-panel
          configurations.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div
        class="mt-14 grid items-stretch gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr_auto_1fr_auto_1fr]"
      >

        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-slate-400">
            01
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Rooftop Input
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Roof imagery and geometric information used as the basis for
            analysis.
          </p>

        </article>


        <div class="hidden items-center text-slate-300 lg:flex">
          →
        </div>


        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-slate-400">
            02
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Image Processing
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Computer-vision operations extract usable rooftop regions and
            structural boundaries.
          </p>

        </article>


        <div class="hidden items-center text-slate-300 lg:flex">
          →
        </div>


        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-slate-400">
            03
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Layout Optimization
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Candidate panel configurations are evaluated under geometric and
            placement constraints.
          </p>

        </article>


        <div class="hidden items-center text-slate-300 lg:flex">
          →
        </div>


        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-slate-400">
            04
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Engineering Output
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Estimated panel placement, orientation and potential energy
            production.
          </p>

        </article>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- COMPUTER VISION -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>
          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            Computer Vision
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Extracting useful geometric information from rooftop imagery.
          </h2>
        </div>


        <div>

          <p class="leading-8 text-slate-600">
            Image-processing operations were used to transform roof imagery
            into geometric information that could later be consumed by the
            optimization stage.
          </p>


          <div class="mt-10 space-y-8">

            <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-[50px_1fr]">

              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
                01
              </p>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-950">
                  Image preprocessing
                </h3>

                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
                  Input imagery was prepared for analysis using Python-based
                  image-processing tools.
                </p>
              </div>

            </div>


            <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-[50px_1fr]">

              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
                02
              </p>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-950">
                  Region identification
                </h3>

                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
                  Rooftop boundaries and usable regions were identified so that
                  geometric constraints could be represented computationally.
                </p>
              </div>

            </div>


            <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-[50px_1fr]">

              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
                03
              </p>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-950">
                  Geometric representation
                </h3>

                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
                  Visual information was converted into structured geometric
                  data for use by the placement algorithm.
                </p>
              </div>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- OPTIMIZATION -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>

          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            Optimization
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Searching for feasible photovoltaic layouts.
          </h2>

        </div>


        <div class="space-y-6 leading-8 text-slate-600">

          <p>
            Once the rooftop geometry was represented computationally, panel
            placement could be formulated as a constrained optimization
            problem.
          </p>

          <p>
            Candidate layouts needed to respect the usable roof region while
            considering panel dimensions, orientation and available space.
          </p>

          <p>
            The optimization stage was designed to identify configurations that
            could increase useful rooftop coverage while remaining physically
            feasible.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- OBJECTIVES -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="max-w-3xl">

        <p
          class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
        >
          Optimization Objectives
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
        >
          Balancing geometric feasibility and photovoltaic potential.
        </h2>

      </div>


      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">

        <article>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            01
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Feasible placement
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Panels must remain within valid rooftop regions and satisfy
            geometric constraints.
          </p>

        </article>


        <article>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            02
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Rooftop utilization
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Candidate layouts seek to make effective use of available rooftop
            surface.
          </p>

        </article>


        <article>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            03
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Energy estimation
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Panel placement and orientation can be connected with expected
            photovoltaic energy production.
          </p>

        </article>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ENGINEERING APPLICATION -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>

          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            Engineering Application
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Computer vision as part of an engineering decision-support tool.
          </h2>

        </div>


        <div class="space-y-6 leading-8 text-slate-600">

          <p>
            A key aspect of the project was connecting computer-vision methods
            with an engineering objective rather than treating image analysis
            as an isolated task.
          </p>

          <p>
            Image processing provided the geometric representation, while the
            optimization stage transformed that representation into practical
            layout candidates.
          </p>

          <p>
            This combination made the workflow suitable for integration into
            interactive engineering applications.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- MECSIMCALC -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>

          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            Research Environment
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Python engineering applications with MecSimCalc.
          </h2>

        </div>


        <div class="space-y-6 leading-8 text-slate-600">

          <p>
            The project was developed as part of the University of Alberta
            Research Experience, where Python engineering applications were
            implemented using the MecSimCalc platform.
          </p>

          <p>
            In parallel with the rooftop-analysis project, interactive
            engineering applications were developed to automate exercises and
            provide immediate feedback to students.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- VISUAL PLACEHOLDER -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="max-w-3xl">

        <p
          class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
        >
          Visualization
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
        >
          From rooftop image to optimized panel layout.
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 leading-8 text-slate-600">
          A visual example of the image-processing and panel-placement pipeline
          will be included here.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div
        class="mt-12 flex min-h-[380px] items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-white"
      >

        <div class="max-w-sm px-8 text-center">

          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700">
            Rooftop analysis visualization
          </p>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Original image → detected roof region → optimized photovoltaic
            layout.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- TECH STACK -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">

        <div>

          <p
            class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
          >
            Technology
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
          >
            Technical stack
          </h2>

        </div>


        <div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">

          <div>

            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950">
              Programming
            </p>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
              Python
            </p>

          </div>


          <div>

            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950">
              Computer Vision
            </p>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
              OpenCV · scikit-image
            </p>

          </div>


          <div>

            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950">
              Methods
            </p>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
              Image processing · Geometric analysis · Optimization
            </p>

          </div>


          <div>

            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950">
              Engineering Platform
            </p>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
              MecSimCalc
            </p>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- WHAT I LEARNED -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-24 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div class="max-w-3xl">

        <p
          class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500"
        >
          Technical Takeaways
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950"
        >
          Combining algorithms around the engineering problem.
        </h2>

      </div>


      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">

        <article>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            01
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Vision is only one stage
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Detecting geometric information becomes more valuable when the
            output is structured for downstream decision-making.
          </p>

        </article>


        <article>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            02
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Constraints matter
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
            A mathematically attractive layout is only useful if it also
            satisfies physical and geometric constraints.
          </p>

        </article>


        <article>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            03
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">
            Engineering + computation
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
            The project reinforced the value of combining domain knowledge with
            computational tools instead of treating them separately.
          </p>

        </article>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- NEXT PROJECT -->

    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-slate-200 px-6 py-20 lg:px-8"
    >

      <div
        class="flex flex-col gap-8 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between"
      >

        <div>

          <p
            class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-400"
          >
            Next Project
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-950"
          >
            Part-of-Speech Tagging with HMM and CRF
          </h2>

        </div>


        <a
          href="/projects/nlp-hmm-crf"
          class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900"
        >
          View project →
        </a>

      </div>

    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />

</BaseLayout>